claim.claim-text:
a body having a distal end, a proximal end, and a longitudinal axis extending therethrough;
a plasma arc exit orifice at the distal end of the body;
a cooling means centrally located on an exterior surface of the body between the distal end and the proximal end, the cooling means circumferentially oriented about the body;
the cooling means having an inlet means for receiving a liquid coolant and an outlet means for redirecting the liquid coolant radially outward in a laminar flow pattern;
the inlet means and the outlet means being axially spaced from one another;
a first sealing member on the exterior surface of the body and located between the distal end of the body and the outlet means; and
a second sealing member on the exterior surface of the body and located between the inlet means and the proximal end of the body; and
the cooling means is configured such that the liquid coolant flow through the cooling means forms a substantially laminar flow, such that the liquid coolant entering the inlet means does not substantially intermingle with the liquid coolant exiting from the outlet means, and the axial liquid flow from the inlet means to the outlet means is substantially even around a circumference of the nozzle.
